-- title:
--   A uniform tame generator of inertia modulo p^m-th powers
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime number and let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` which lies over $q$ in the sense that the image of $q$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ belongs to `P.nonunits`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $P$. Write $I_P$ for `P.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{alg}} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ obtained as the image of the inertia subgroup of $P$ inside the decomposition subgroup of $P$ under the inclusion of that decomposition subgroup into the full automorphism group. The assertion is that there is a single element $\gamma \in I_P$ with the following uniform property: for every prime $p$ with $p \neq q$, every natural number $m$, and every $\tau \in I_P$, there are a natural number $j$ and elements $x, w \in I_P$ such that $\tau = \gamma^{j}\, x^{p^m}\, w^{p^m}$. Thus $\gamma$ alone generates $I_P$ modulo the subgroup generated by $p^m$-th powers of inertia elements, simultaneously for all $p \neq q$ and all $m$; the exponent $j$ and the elements $x, w$ may depend on $p$, $m$ and $\tau$, while $\gamma$ may not.
--
--   This records the pro-cyclicity of the tame quotient of the inertia group at a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $q$, in the form of a generator valid uniformly in the auxiliary prime $p \neq q$ and the level $p^m$. It is used in the analysis of inertia acting on Tate modules and on cuspidal divisor classes of modular curves, namely by [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_forall_mem_toricPts_exists_smul_sub_eq_of_coprime_of_abelJacobiPin_of_atkinLehner`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.exists_forall_mem_toricPts_exists_smul_sub_eq_of_coprime_of_abelJacobiPin_of_atkinLehner) and [`ModularCurve.JH.exists_pow_smul_mem_span_inertia_sub_sup_old_of_rep_eq_self_tateModule_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JH.exists_pow_smul_mem_span_inertia_sub_sup_old_of_rep_eq_self_tateModule_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd).
